1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,320
Someone bought almost every Texas lottery combo and won ninety-five million.

2
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:07,800
And it wasn't even the first time. Let's go back to Virginia, nineteen ninety-two.

3
00:00:09,400 --> 00:00:13,880
An Australian fund tried to buy every single ticket, over five million of them.

4
00:00:14,320 --> 00:00:18,280
They hit the jackpot: twenty-seven million dollars, a state record.

5
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:21,080
Tap the heart if you'd have done the exact same thing.

6
00:00:21,580 --> 00:00:25,140
But there was a catch. Tickets had to be bought at a licensed store.

7
00:00:25,540 --> 00:00:28,200
And these guys? They had millions printed in bulk.

8
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:34,000
So Virginia investigated. Three weeks later, nobody could prove the winning ticket broke a rule.

9
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:38,860
So they paid. About one point three million a year, for twenty years.

10
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:42,260
That's like twenty normal salaries, every single year.

11
00:00:42,740 --> 00:00:45,440
Send this to the friend who still buys one ticket and prays.

12
00:00:46,220 --> 00:00:49,180
Then Virginia panicked and rushed in rules against bulk buying.

13
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:53,380
Didn't matter. Thirty-one years later, Texas got hit the same way.

14
00:00:53,760 --> 00:00:56,720
Follow if you're here for the math. And how did Texas take it?

15
00:00:56,720 --> 00:01:00,440
It got so messy that the state shut down its whole lottery commission.

16
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:03,860
Should buying every combo be legal? Yes or no.

